    "name": "James P. Kelleher Rose Garden",
    "why": "Planted rose beds of the James P. Kelleher Rose Garden. The USGS NAIP aerial photograph of 7 July 2023 shows concentric gravel rings with rose beds between and outside them, a mown lawn disc 8.1 m in radius at the centre (measured from the photograph about the rings' fitted centre) and a long rectangular lawn panel inside the rectangular path with a bed band about 1.8 m wide along its edges. The garden polygon w29078412 was drawn as plain ground; it is redrawn as planted beds with the two lawns cut out. The gravel paths (w546932357, w546932358, w546932361 and others) are drawn over the beds.",
